@startuml fig9-members
!include style.iuml
title Figure 9 (new): Remove a member or leave a group (optional extension, R10; A6, D9)

actor "Owner / Member" as User
participant ":MembersFragment /\n:GroupDetailActivity" as UI
participant ":ConfirmDialog" as CD
participant ":GroupViewModel" as VM
participant ":TransactionRepository" as TR
participant ":BalanceCalculator" as BC
participant ":GroupRepository" as GR
participant "db : FirebaseFirestore\n(+ security rules)" as DB

alt Owner removes a member
  User -> UI : ⋮ next to a member → Remove from group
  UI -> CD : show()
  CD -> VM : removeMember(uid)
  VM -> VM : isOwner()? uid is a member\nand not the owner?
else Member (not the owner) leaves
  User -> UI : menu → Leave group
  UI -> CD : show()
  CD -> VM : leaveGroup()
  VM -> VM : current user is not the owner?\n(the owner must transfer ownership first)
end
VM -> VM : removeIfSettled(current, uid, unsettledPrefix, onRemoved)\n(uid = the member removed, or the current user)
VM -> TR : getTransactions(groupId, cb)
TR -> DB : get groups/{groupId}/transactions
DB --> TR : documents
TR --> VM : cb.onSuccess(transactions)
VM -> BC : computeTotals(uid, memberIds, transactions)
BC --> VM : {totalToPay, totalToReceive}
alt not settled up (either total ≠ 0)
  VM --> UI : error (Event): "… still owes or is owed $X in this group. Settle up first."\n(when leaving: "You still owe or are owed $X …")
  UI --> User : snackbar with the error
else settled up with everyone
  VM -> GR : removeMember(groupId, uid, cb)
  GR -> DB : update memberIds = arrayRemove(uid)
  note right of DB
    NEW rules: the owner may remove others but
    must stay a member; any other member may
    remove only themselves and change nothing else
  end note
  DB --> GR : ok
  GR --> VM : cb.onSuccess(null)
  VM --> UI : group and member list updated, info (Event) / leftGroup (Event)
  UI --> User : snackbar "… was removed from the group" /\nToast "You left the group", back to the group list
end
note over UI, DB
  Old transactions keep the former member's id; History and Details load their names through FormerMembers.
  A transaction that involves a former member can still be deleted by its creator but no longer edited.
end note

legend bottom left
New interaction (not in Project 2.2).
endlegend
@enduml
